The problem states that Susan made 100 cookies. Her husband ate 4 cookies, so the number of cookies left is 100 - 4 = 96. Susan is going to divide the cookies equally among her 6 nephews. Therefore, each nephew will get 96 / 6 = 16 cookies.

\boxed{16}
